==Dutch==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lang=nl|/ˈsxeː.rə(n)/}}
* {{audio|Nl-scheren (Belgium).ogg|audio (Belgium)|lang=nl}}
* {{audio|Nl-scheren.ogg|audio (Netherlands)|lang=nl}}
* {{rhymes|eːrən|lang=nl}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|nl|(s)ker}}
From {{inh|nl|dum|scheren}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|skeran}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*skeraną}}, from {{der|nl|ine-pro|*(s)ker-||to cut}}. Akin to Low German {{m|nds|scheren}}, German {{m|de|scheren}}, West Frisian {{m|fy|skeare}}, English {{m|en|shear|}}, Danish {{m|da|skære}}.

===Verb===
{{nl-verb}}

# to [[shave]] (reflexive pronouns are used for self-directed actions)
#:{{ux|nl|hij scheert zich nu|he's shaving now|inline=1}}
#:{{ux|nl|de arts scheerde de huid rond the wond van de patiënt|the doctor shaved the skin around the patient's wound|inline=1}}
# to [[shear]]
#:{{ux|nl|morgen gaan ze de schapen scheren|they will shear the sheep tomorrow|inline=1}}

